  "mapping": {
    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "Aurabot's identity is a party-support buff-projector — zero personal damage, output = ALLIES' amplified power — and it is explicitly useless solo. The engine is solo-scope, so the kit's entire purpose has no lane: there are no allies to buff. Additionally the ~100% reservation exceeds the engine's 0.75 LOCKED reservation cap. Mapped the aura shell + clamped reserve, but a player of the original would find the build does literally nothing in solo — the ally-projection that IS the kit cannot be expressed. Docketed as out-of-solo-scope.",
    "grade": "GAPPED",
    "kit_id": "poe1-aurabot",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "GAPPED on IDENTITY: Aurabot's entire purpose is projecting auras onto ALLIES to multiply PARTY output — it is strictly multiplayer and useless solo (source: 'useless solo', mech_note). The engine is solo-scope; there is no ally to receive the buff, so the kit's reason-for-existing has no lane. Distinct from aurastacker (self-stacking, next kit) — Aurabot uses Generosity to share to allies NOT self. TWO gaps docketed: (1) ally-buff-projection role has no solo-scope lane; (2) Aurabot reserves ~100% of pool, EXCEEDING the engine's reservation_percent 0.75 LOCKED cap — clamped in the map, noting the source exceeds it. NETWORK_AMPLIFIER/RESONANCE_LOOP are the nearest T4s (aura-network amps) but they model SELF-amplification, not ally-projection. Mapped the shell (aura geometry + clamped full-reserve) as MAPPED_DOCKET.",
      "motion_frame": "walking buff-station: no personal offense; the player's job is to keep allies inside a large aura radius — a role that does not exist in solo scope",
